cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this verification artifact, please cite the specific archived version you
  checked, not the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI.
title: >-
  krotenheerdt-sequence: machine-checked companion to "The three-dimensional Krötenheerdt
  sequence and its vanishing point"
abstract: >-
  The verification artifact for the paper's claims: the stacking model of honeycombs by cubes
  and prisms with two prism directions, the symmetries of a stacking word, and the exact
  enumeration of the words with every cut the paper proves; the facts of the species table
  the structure theorems use; the slab world; the census of the rows k = 2, 3, 4; the
  prismatic lifts, with the planar Krötenheerdt sequence re-derived by a SAT assembler; and
  the enumeration of the rows k = 4 to 10 with the dossier of every class from k = 5 on. The
  sequence of k-uniform Krötenheerdt honeycombs of Euclidean 3-space is 28, 57, 119, 146,
  122, 78, 18, 2 and vanishes from k = 9 on. All shared machinery is the pinned research-core
  library.
